From 7789ca7ba806e97163ce05d28a8fc34ba5a2bcf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:28:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Texture bindings: descriptors read in place, handles one page
 walk per page; one pipeline lookup

DescriptorTable::Read translated the pool's GPU address for every descriptor (twice per texture
per draw: the texture's and the sampler's). It now keeps the pool's host range (MemoryManager::
GetSpan over the whole limit, when contiguous) and reads in place, working it out again when the
pool's address or limit changes or after any GPU or device mapping change: a new
Core::gpu_mapping_generation, bumped by MemoryManager::PageTableOp/BigPageTableOp and
DeviceMemoryManager::Map/Unmap. GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureImpl keeps the last 4 KiB GPU page's
host pointer while reading a draw's texture handles. (Ryujinx reads a stage's handles from one
span and skips unchanged bindings.)

RasterizerVulkan::UpdateDynamicStates asked the pipeline cache for the current pipeline again
(vertex input, alpha to coverage/one): PrepareDraw now passes the draw's (DrawPipeline()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
